{
  "requirement": "The method is declared under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.load_evidence`.\n\n`load_evidence` captures the source identity and criterion path while constructing\nits future. It retains no reference to the criterion value while storage is\npending, so the criterion needs no `Sync` bound. It loads the complete record and\ndecodes its output under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`.\nVersion and input comparison are separate steps.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.check_node`. I did not read the implementation. The assessment rests on the supplied test source.\n\n**No `Sync` bound and early capture.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` passes `validator.load_evidence(&descriptor)` through a `send(...)` helper. By its name, that helper requires the future to be `Send`. The descriptor is a `Review` that holds a `Cell` (`descriptor_reads`), so it is not `Sync`. A future that kept `&criterion` across a storage await, or held it from construction until the first poll, would not be `Send`. The test also asserts `descriptor_reads == 1` and a correct loaded output. This is my reading of how `send` and `Review` work, because I did not open the helper definitions.\n\n**Loading the complete record.**\n- `fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` loads a saved record. It checks `output`, `source_node_id`, `criterion_path`, `version` and `dependencies` against the stored value.\n- It also checks that a missing record returns `Ok(None)`.\n- `fn[wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes]` shows that a different criterion path or source node returns `None`. Together these show that the captured source identity and criterion path locate the record.\n- `fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` loads a record with outgoing-edge dependencies and compares them.\n\n**Decoding output under `record.output`.**\n- `fn[typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence]` and `tests/storage.rs#fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]` assert `ValidationError::Output` for an output that cannot decode. This holds even when the version or inputs are stale.\n- The storage test also asserts that the file is unchanged and that no re-execution happened.\n- The malformed-record and storage-failure cases are covered by `FileStorageError::Json` and `Graph(\"load\")` in `validation_tests.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` and `contracts.rs#fn[loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers]`.\n\n**Version and input comparison as separate steps.**\n- `validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` loads a record saved under `v1` with a `v2` criterion. The load succeeds and returns the old version. `is_compatible_with` is false and `check_inputs` is true. The legacy `None` version case is also covered.\n- `contracts.rs#fn[dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers]` loads successfully while input resolution fails. `check_inputs` then returns `Err`.\n- `fn[changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another]` loads both records and gets different `check_inputs` results.\n- `fn[typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence]` asserts that loading performs no input reads.\n\nThe declaration obligation, \"declared under `load_evidence`\", is a cited requirement and needs no separate test. All tests carry `{test}` markers for the subject.",
